# SCSS Rules

## File Header
```scss
@use 'sass:math';
@use 'sass:map';
@use 'sass:list';
@use 'sass:string';

// =============================================================================
// ${fileName}
// =============================================================================
//
// ${fileDescription}
//
// @author ${author}
// @since ${date}
// =============================================================================
```

## Function Documentation
```scss
/// ${functionDescription}
/// 
/// @param {${paramType}} ${paramName} - ${paramDescription}
/// @returns {${returnType}} - ${returnDescription}
@function ${functionName}($${paramName}) {
  ${body}
}
```

## Mixin Documentation
```scss
/// ${mixinDescription}
/// 
/// @param {${paramType}} ${paramName} - ${paramDescription}
/// @content - ${contentDescription}
/// 
/// @returns {void} - ${returnDescription}
@mixin ${mixinName}($${paramName}) {
  ${body}
}
```

## Style Rules
- Indentation: 2 spaces
- Max line length: 80 characters
- Require leading underscore for partials
- Require var prefix for variables
- Sort order: SMACSS

## Property Order
1. Position
2. Display
3. Box-sizing
4. Width
5. Height
6. Margin
7. Padding
8. Border
9. Background
10. Color
11. Font
12. Text

## Best Practices
- Use triple-slash comments (`///`) for documentation
- Include parameter types and descriptions
- Always document return values
- Group related properties together
- Use meaningful variable names
- Follow BEM naming convention for classes
